  "body": "Found while surveying #339 and confirmed on main with a scratch test.\n\n**What happens:** `bands_vs_fixtures` (law c2) puts every band column at `min(from.z, to.z)` for a move. On a ramp, the stack at the high end sits higher than that. Two parts go unjudged: the top of the stack there, and the flute-radius ring above the flute's top at the low end.\n\n**Repro:** a ramp from z 0 to z 40, with a clamp arm at z 100..120 over the high end and the holder top at 130 there. No hit is reported.\n\n**Why P0:** a crash into workholding that the post gate lets through.\n\n**Done means:** each band is judged over its true z span along the move, so the repro reports `FixtureHit` (Holder) and blocks the post. Level moves keep their verdicts, and every existing fixture suite stays green.\n\nRelated: #339 (triage there).",
